        "subject": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: fix races with the failover thread",
        "message": "LU-6132 o2iblnd: fix races with the failover thread\n\nThe failover thread uses a dev and the pools of its nets with no\nref. A net shutdown during a failover can free them. The dev destroy\nand the net shutdown now wait until the thread clears ibd_failover.\n\nThe thread uses the netns of the first NI for all devs. That NI can\nshut down first. Each dev now holds a ref on the netns of the NI\nthat created it.\n\nkiblnd_startup() adds a dev to kib_devs with no lock. Add it under\nkib_global_lock. kiblnd_get_dev_prio() reads ibd_hdev with no lock.\nIt now reads a ref-counted DMA device under RCU.\n\nFixes: 7b442f1a4371 (\"b=20153 add IB bonding failover support to o2iblnd\")\nFixes: 93b08edfb1c6 (\"LU-12236 lnet: support non-default network namespace\")\nFixes: a7a889f77cec (\"LU-14798 lnet: add LNet GPU Direct Support\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ia9122e4766240185124527789ac2f031e280ea08\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
